# Plan: PCA on forms of capital — Younger Bronze Age (1100-500 BCE)

## Observations
- capital.csv: 39 rows × 15 cols, 100-year slices BCE 4300→500.
- Numeric Z-values use European decimal commas (quoted). Must convert.
- YBA = group with BCE ∈ [500, 1100] (7 slices: 1100, 1000, 900, 800, 700, 600, 500).
- 12 capital features: ZAxtSchwert, ZDolch, Zhausgr, ZCU_AU, Zamber, ZMonument, ZHort, ZSichel, ZBeil, ZMW, ZKeform, Zkeverz.
- ZSichel and ZKeform are constant across YBA (zero variance) — drop for PCA.
- 1100 BCE is an upper outlier vs. later YBA slices.

## Pilot PCA summary (full 39-row, standardized)
- PC1 = 30.3% variance; positive loadings on most forms of capital (general wealth/intensity axis).
- YBA PC1: 1100 ≈ 4.45; 1000 ≈ 2.15; 900 ≈ 1.63; 800 ≈ 1.89; 700 ≈ 1.23; 600 ≈ 0.80; 500 ≈ 0.78.
- Mean(1000-500) ≈ 1.41; 1100 BCE is well above the entire YBA range.

## Proposed workflow
1. Load capital.csv with European-decimal parsing.
2. Filter YBA (BCE 1100→500); drop ZSichel, ZKeform (constant in YBA).
3. Standardize features (z-score within YBA). PCA via SVD on the standardized matrix.
4. Orient PC1 so higher = more capital; record (BCE, PC1).
5. Compare PC1(1100) with PC1(1000-500) statistics and tabulate.
6. Save executed analysis/notebook to artifacts.analysis (per contract).
